SHA verified against `context.json` and the supplied value before reading. No sibling review was opened (a `future.md` appeared mid-write from a parallel evaluator; left unread).

**Verdict:** `revise` — trust strained, value high, delight clear_hit. **3 blockers, 5 concerns.**

**Strongest hit:** the shift-bell paragraph — *"He already spent four years of his life performing somebody else's script on somebody else's clock... The fans handing him the rizz prompt mean it as tribute. What he hears is a shift bell."* Every fan has seen him deflect the rizz question a hundred times; nobody has connected it to the Army. That plus *"His mother's sentence outlasted his own"* and *"The factory got twenty-nine days"* are the reasons this piece deserves to exist, and I flagged them for byte-identical protection during any repair.

**Highest-priority concern (blocker FAN-R1):** the draft says Duke "sat in the inaugural class himself the year before, as a student." His own channel published *"Being A Professor At Streamer University"* on 2025-05-23 and Part 2 on 2025-05-26 — I confirmed both uploads independently of the packet. The only support for the student reading is Rolling Stone preview copy. It's fan-checkable in a minute, and it sits inside the piece's most original section. The true fact is also the better paragraph: a man who refuses "rizz," "Unc," and "aura" has now accepted "Professor" twice.

The other two blockers: *"The circle has billed him exactly once"* is false as of this date (Aug 2025 San Antonio arrest with Kai; $1M suit naming him and AMP reported June 2026) — repairable by dropping the count without importing legal detail, per the packet's own constraint. And the 8w9 wing argument ("slow to escalate," "never as rants," "an 8w7 would have turned the friction into content") is contradicted by the aura-farming slam the packet quotes and by the November 11, 2025 episode where Duke took RaKai's ~$100K chain and had an on-stream shoving match with Tylil — which is *literally* turning friction into content. That last item came from my own research, not the packet; I sourced it across four outlets and wrote the finding so its core survives even if the episode is judged too clip-tier to narrate.

The pattern underneath all three: this article's Duke is the February 2024 Duke, and it doesn't say so.
